Fixed dev/test RSA-2048 broker signing keypair (the dev "ProveKey") — the
PRIVATE half, loaded by config/environments/{development,test}.rb into
Rails.configuration.x.prove.key_pem when PROVE_KEY_PEM is unset. Fixed (not
per-boot ephemeral) so a broker restart keeps the key a hand-wired local
operator has pinned; the two-server harnesses need no fixed value (they fetch
the public half from the running broker's GET /prove_key.pem, K-650).

DO NOT use in production: this file ships world-readable in a public repo, so
anyone could forge attestations signed with it. Production refuses to boot
without an explicit PROVE_KEY_PEM (config/environments/production.rb, K-673).
Generated once: ruby -ropenssl -e "puts OpenSSL::PKey::RSA.new(2048).to_pem"
(OpenSSL tolerates this text preamble when parsing the PEM below.)

